#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example illustrates how to add Live Video when running in Simulink. This example was copied from a lengthy run, {Driver Speed from Path Preview} > Speed Control from Driver Path.
#
#To view the live video:
#(1) click "Send to Simulink". VS Visualizer will start, but the vehicle parts will not be located correctly.
#
#(2) click the Play button in Simulink to run the simulation.  Once the run starts, the video will show the status.
#
#If you do not see a button in this screen "Start Live Video", please check Tools > License Settings and make sure the "CarSim Extra Live Animator" option is checked.
#
#To use Live Video for another run:
#(1) Select "Models: Simulink" and link to a Simulink model. For this example, the blue link is {Live Video} > Base Model. Go to this dataset for notes on enabling live animation.
#
#(2) When the link is made to a Simulink model, three controls appear involving live video. The number of live cameras should be set to 1.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

